Local patch one_sided_jerk_v1 for COPP 0.2.2.

Adds ConstraintSide (Both/Left/Right) so a third-order jerk row can be
attached to only one adjacent interval, implementing the paper's one-sided
constraints (Eqs. 7c-d) at polynomial knots where the left and right path
derivatives differ. Both is the default, so existing C, C++ and Robot
callers keep their current two-sided behaviour.

Also restricts jerk linearization to active rows, fixing a shape mismatch
for nonuniform row counts.

